<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
    <div class="glass-card p-8 md:p-12 rounded-2xl border-t-4 border-[#D4AF37]">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#D4AF37] mb-3">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 brand-font">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: August 29, 2026. This privacy policy is published by Future Music Collective (Fox Parton) for futuremusic.online and the Blockbuilder app on the Meta Horizon Store.</p>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed font-light">
            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Who we are</h2>
                <p>Future Music Collective operates the website at <a class="text-[#D4AF37] underline" href="https://futuremusic.online">https://futuremusic.online</a> and the Blockbuilder virtual reality workshop distributed on the Meta Horizon Store. This page explains what data we collect, how we use it, and how you can ask us to delete it.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">What data we collect</h2>
                <p class="mb-3">We collect only what we need to run the site, process purchases, and load the Blockbuilder Quest app:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Account data</strong> if you register on the website: name or display name, email address, and a hashed password. We do not store your raw password.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Purchase data</strong> if you buy merch or unlock the browser version of Blockbuild: items, amounts, and fulfillment details. Card numbers are processed by Stripe. We do not see or store full payment-card numbers.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Contact messages</strong> you send through our contact form: name, email, subject, and message body.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Cookies and similar storage</strong> used to keep you logged in, remember a cart, or remember that you unlocked Blockbuild in the browser (<code class="text-white">bb_unlock</code>).</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Technical logs</strong> when you load our pages: IP address, date and time, requested URL, referrer, and browser or headset user-agent. These are ordinary web-server logs. The Blockbuilder Quest app is a native install; it does not load the website to play.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Advertising data on some website pages</strong> (not inside the Quest app): Google AdSense and similar partners may set cookies and collect device identifiers as described in their own policies.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Blockbuilder on Meta Quest</h2>
                <p>The Quest version of Blockbuilder is a native workshop app. Your brick maps and save slots are stored locally on the headset. We do not receive those builds unless you send them to us. The Quest app does not require an account, does not show ads, and does not currently process in-app payments through us. Store purchases are processed by Meta.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">How we use data</h2>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website and Blockbuilder.</li>
                    <li>To create and maintain your account if you register.</li>
                    <li>To process orders, send receipts, and unlock paid browser content you bought.</li>
                    <li>To answer messages you send us.</li>
                    <li>To diagnose errors, prevent abuse, and meet legal obligations.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mt-3">We do not sell your personal information. We do not use Blockbuilder save files for advertising.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Who else sees data</h2>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Hosting and delivery</strong> for futuremusic.online (currently Google Cloud Run and related infrastructure).</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Stripe</strong> for payment processing on the website.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Email delivery</strong> to receive contact-form messages.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Meta</strong> if you install Blockbuilder from the Meta Horizon Store. Meta’s own platform policies and privacy policy apply to your Meta account, headset telemetry, and store purchases.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-white">Advertising partners</strong> on some website pages, as noted above. The Quest app does not include those partners.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">How long we keep data</h2>
                <p>Account and order records are kept while the account is open and for a limited period afterward as needed for accounting, chargebacks, and legal requirements. Server logs are rotated on a routine schedule. Contact messages are kept long enough to reply and follow up. Local Blockbuilder saves remain on your device until you clear them or uninstall the app.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">How to request deletion of your data</h2>
                <p class="mb-3">You may request that we delete personal data we have collected or stored about you. To do that:</p>
                <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
                    <li>Open <a class="text-[#D4AF37] underline" href="/contact">https://futuremusic.online/contact</a>.</li>
                    <li>Send a message that includes the email you used with us and the words “delete my data” or “privacy deletion request.”</li>
                    <li>We will confirm and delete account records, contact messages, and other personal data we control, except information we must retain for legal, security, or accounting reasons (for example, a paid invoice).</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="mt-3">You can also delete locally stored Blockbuilder maps yourself by clearing the app’s data on the headset or uninstalling Blockbuilder. If you have a website account, the same contact request can close the account.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Children</h2>
                <p>The website is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has given us personal information, contact us using the deletion steps above and we will delete it.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Changes</h2>
                <p>We may update this privacy policy. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do. Continued use of the site or Blockbuilder after an update means you have read the revised policy.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl text-[#D4AF37] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Contact</h2>
                <p>Questions about this privacy policy, data collection, or deletion: <a class="text-[#D4AF37] underline" href="/contact">https://futuremusic.online/contact</a>. Terms of service: <a class="text-[#D4AF37] underline" href="/terms">https://futuremusic.online/terms</a>.</p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
